{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559853-dragons-becoming-gods","id":1559853,"title":"Dragons becoming Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-09T05:41:46-07:00","id":1559853,"title":"Dragons becoming Gods","content":"I gave a game where my players are half way through there apotheosis. I have player playing a Dragon and I'm trying to figure out how dragons becom Gods.<br /> on page 84 in the Scion God book it says:<br /> Dragons who have become part of Pantheons and bear Divine Mantles generally use the rules for Gods, unless they\u2019re actively trying to shed the Mantle and act outside of Godly nature. <br /> <br /> It's unclear to me what that is surpose to mean.<br /> Does the Dragon get Legend and perviews and loose thier Inheritance? <br /> or are they working with the Draconic Power stat?<br /> (In the Dragon Companion book, it says they start at Draconic Power 5, when they resch Inheritance 10...).<br /> <br /> My first thought was to let the dragon use his Inheritance like Legend, when he reached 9 and had a Mantle and pantheon. <br /> And let him have a single or two perviews, through relics, but no boons. To avoid too mush bouble dipping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3356-kalle","name":"Kalle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T15:17:51-07:00","id":1559856,"title":"","content":"Iirc this is discussed in the god companion book, though i can't remember how much depth they go into it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T00:58:50-07:00","id":1559914,"title":"","content":"They don't go into much more depth. Dragon Companion, page 32 Dragons In Divine Realm Play.<br /> Draconic Power is not really explaned and the text on Dragons becomming Gods, is the same as in the Scion God book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3356-kalle","name":"Kalle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T04:21:02-07:00","id":1559918,"title":"","content":"It is implied that Fatebinding is involved, in the original Dragon book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T07:36:15-07:00","id":1559921,"title":"","content":"Humans ascending to become gods is kind of overdone at this point.<br /> <br /> Humans evolving into dragons, though? Now that's some original content!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T05:48:06-07:00","id":1561158,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you wanna get technical, eastern dragons (particularly China / Japan) are often considered to be minor divinities. <br /> <br /> There are also some members of the eastern pantheons (Gods and Titans) who choose to take on the appearance of dragons. Just because you're associated with humans, doesn't mean you have to look the part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}